1. **The bottleneck is outside the micro-kernel.** Static buffers and per-task A packing gave no gain, so overhead and scaling are what limit speed. First measure single-thread GFLOP/s. If one core reaches about 80% of its FMA peak, the kernel is fine and threading is the problem.

